== New Results and third experiment to understand Wikipedia citation usage ==

Hi everyone,

We  performed some analysis of the [[Wikipedia:Village pump (miscellaneous)/Archive 59#Results and new experiment to understand Wikipedia citation usage| data collected last October]] reflecting readers' interactions with references in English Wikipedia. Please find our first analysis of this data in [[m:Research:Characterizing_Wikipedia_Citation_Usage/Second_Round_of_Analysis|our project page]]. This work is part of the [[m:Research:Characterizing_Wikipedia_Citation_Usage | "Citation Usage"]] research project, which aims to understand how Wikipedia readers interact with citations, and the role of external citations in Wikipedia reading. The analysis resulting from this project could inform the editor and tool developer communities about the usage (or not) of citations by Wikipedia readers.

After the second round of data collection, which ended on 2018-25-10, we have modified the code behind our instrumentation to address a number of bugs related to specific fields of the Schema, and we will start a second round of data collection next Thursday, March 21st. The structure is similar to last round of data collection: we will collect data that captures readers' (not logged-in users only) page views, as well as their interactions with references and footnotes. We will initially sample 1–15% of the traffic to validate the data quality, then turn at 100% sampling rate for a period of one month. All details can be found at [[phab:T212937 |this task]].

To follow the progress of the project and monitor our research results, please also look at [[phab:T199188 | this task]]. If you are interested to know more, or if you have any question, or any observation, please ping me or leave a message on the project page! 
