== Name of Wikidata ID parameter in templates ==

We have several templates that take a Wikidata ID ("QID") as a parameter; and those parameters don't have a standard name. For example:

* {{tl|Interlanguage link}} - {{para|WD}}
* {{tl|Wikidata}} - {{para|eid}}
* {{tl|Public art row}} - {{para|wikidata}}
* {{tl|Infobox gene}} - {{para|QID}}
* {{tl|EditAtWikidata}} - {{para|qid}}

Can we rationalise these? QID or qid seem to be the most common. <span class="vcard"><span class="fn">[[User:Pigsonthewing|Andy Mabbett]]</span> (<span class="nickname">Pigsonthewing</span>); [[User talk:Pigsonthewing|Talk to Andy]]; [[Special:Contributions/Pigsonthewing|Andy's edits]]</span> 12:44, 2 April 2019 (UTC)
